<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The tasbih card, hand-built out of framework views - approved Design 1.

  Why this is not a Glance composition
  =============================================
  A counter has to repaint on every bead. On this project's test device (POCO
  X7 Pro, Android 16, HyperOS V816) a Glance widget composes exactly ONCE per
  process: GlanceAppWidget.update() on an already-open session re-applies the
  session's cached tree and never re-runs provideGlance. Measured with a
  compose log inside provideContent: four taps, four paint calls, one
  composition, and the card sat on the first tap's number until the process
  was killed. That is the "clicks do not work" report, and no amount of tuning
  inside the composition could reach it.

  A hand-written RemoteViews has no session to go stale: a tap is
  partiallyUpdateAppWidget with only the setters that changed, which the
  launcher merges into the view it already has - no re-inflation, no
  composition, a few hundred bytes across the binder instead of ~1 MB of
  bitmaps.

  FULLY RESPONSIVE (brief 2026-11-04)
  ===================================
  «اگر کوچکش کنم عناصر هم به تبعیت کوچک شوند»: there is deliberately NO fixed
  dp size, padding or margin left in this file. Everything is wrap_content or
  0 dp with a weight, and TasbihNativeViews.bindMetrics() sets every padding,
  every text size, every icon bitmap and the ring bitmap from ONE `scale`
  derived from AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetOptions(). The id list below is
  the contract: every id is bound by bindMetrics (full render) or bindState
  (full + tap render).

  Sizes are owned by BITMAPS and by setViewPadding (raw pixels), NOT by
  setViewLayoutWidth/Height. On this launcher setViewLayoutWidth(id, dp, 0)
  landed as PIXELS - a 119 dp ring box rendered as 117 px (36 dp), which was
  the «دایره خیلی کوچک» report. A bitmap's intrinsic size and setViewPadding
  cannot be re-interpreted by a host.

  THE ORDER (brief 2026-11-07, «_v2»)
  ==================================
  «سبحان الله بالا باشد و ذکر ۱ از ۸ پایینش باشد، و از ۱۰۰ زیر دایره باشد نه
  روی دایره». The card reads, top to bottom:

    1. the dhikr name            (tasbih_dhikr)
    2. the «ذکر N از M» pill     (tasbih_pill_row / tasbih_pill_position)
    3. the ring, count inside    (tasbih_ring_area / tasbih_ring / tasbih_count)
    4. the «از N» badge BELOW the ring (tasbih_badge_row / tasbih_badge)
    5. prev / reset / next       (tasbih_controls)

  That is a STRUCTURAL change from v1, where the pill sat above the dhikr and
  the badge was a child of the ring's centre group (drawn ON the circle). A
  launcher recycles the inflated tree when the layout id is unchanged and then
  drops the setters for ids it does not have, so the resource id changes with
  the structure: this file is `_v2` and TasbihNativeViews points at it.

  The «امروز N» pill is GONE (brief: «امروز 10 حذف کنید»). The fixed bands
  around the ring were trimmed (pad 6, gap 5, chip 33, dhikr 12.5 at scale 1)
  so the ring stays the card's one focal point.

  The ring area is ONE square box whose bitmap and its centred count group
  share a FrameLayout, so the number is concentric with the ring at every
  size. The completed-lap tick lives in the badge text, which now hangs under
  the circle instead of sitting inside it.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/tasbih_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:layoutDirection="rtl">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/tasbih_surface"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:scaleType="fitXY" />

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/tasbih_content"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:gravity="center_horizontal"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- 1. The dhikr name — the card's title line. -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/tasbih_dhikr"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:fontFamily="@font/calibri"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:includeFontPadding="false"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textStyle="bold" />

        <!-- 2. «ذکر N از M» — directly UNDER the name (v2; it used to be the
             card's top line). -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/tasbih_pill_row"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:orientation="horizontal">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_pill_position"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_tasbih_pill"
                android:fontFamily="@font/calibri"
                android:maxLines="1" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- 3. The ring. -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:id="@+id/tasbih_ring_area"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1">

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_ring_box"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_gravity="center">

                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/tasbih_ring"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:scaleType="fitXY" />

                <!-- CONCENTRICITY (device-measured 2026-11-04): this group MUST
                     be wrap_content WITH layout_gravity="center". As a
                     match_parent child of a wrap_content FrameLayout, the host
                     re-measured it against the ring-area width and, with the
                     root's RTL direction, placed the number to the RIGHT of the
                     ring. A wrap_content group has no ambiguous second measure
                     pass: its own centre is the FrameLayout's centre, which is
                     the bitmap's centre.

                     v2: the group holds the COUNT only — the badge moved out to
                     its own row under the circle, so nothing pushes the number
                     off the ring's true centre. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/tasbih_ring_center"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:gravity="center_horizontal"
                    android:orientation="vertical">

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/tasbih_count"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:fontFamily="@font/calibri"
                        android:fontFeatureSettings="tnum"
                        android:gravity="center"
                        android:includeFontPadding="false"
                        android:maxLines="1"
                        android:textStyle="bold" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </FrameLayout>
        </FrameLayout>

        <!-- 4. «از N» — BELOW the circle (brief: «از ۱۰۰ زیر دایره باشد نه روی
             دایره»). Its own row, so the ring keeps its full square and the
             badge can never overlap the arc. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/tasbih_badge_row"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:orientation="horizontal">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_badge"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:background="@drawable/widget_tasbih_badge"
                android:fontFamily="@font/calibri"
                android:fontFeatureSettings="tnum"
                android:maxLines="1" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- 5. prev / reset / next. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/tasbih_controls"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="false"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:orientation="horizontal">

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_prev"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/tasbih_prev_chip"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_tasbih_chip">

                    <ImageView
                        android:id="@+id/tasbih_prev_icon"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_gravity="center"
                        android:contentDescription="prev dhikr" />
                </FrameLayout>
            </FrameLayout>

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_reset"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/tasbih_reset_chip"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_tasbih_chip">

                    <ImageView
                        android:id="@+id/tasbih_reset_icon"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_gravity="center"
                        android:contentDescription="reset counter" />
                </FrameLayout>
            </FrameLayout>

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/tasbih_next"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                <FrameLayout
                    android:id="@+id/tasbih_next_chip"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:background="@drawable/widget_tasbih_chip">

                    <ImageView
                        android:id="@+id/tasbih_next_icon"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_gravity="center"
                        android:contentDescription="next dhikr" />
                </FrameLayout>
            </FrameLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
    </LinearLayout>
</FrameLayout>
